.TH MARK-SHOT 1 "August 2026" "Mark Shot 0.1.49" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mark-shot \- capture, select, and annotate screenshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mark-shot
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mark-shot
captures displays or regions, opens images for annotation, pins images, and
provides recording, OCR, code scanning, translation, and upload integrations.
It supports Wayland and X11 desktops.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the program version.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Annotate the complete captured frame without region selection.
.TP
.B \-\-tray
Keep running in the system tray and register supported global shortcuts.
.TP
.BI \-\-pin-image " path"
Open an image directly as a pinned sticker.
.TP
.BI \-\-capture-to " path"
Capture without opening the interface and write to a file or directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-region " x,y,width,height"
Limit a headless capture to logical screen coordinates.
.TP
.BI \-\-display " name"
Capture a named output. This option may be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-list-displays
Print the available outputs as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-xdg-window
Use a regular fullscreen xdg-shell window instead of layer-shell.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug logging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mark-shot/config.json
Per-user configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mark-shot
Per-user models and provider plugins.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mark-shot-ocr (1),
.BR mark-shot-code-scan (1),
.BR mark-shot-translate (1),
.BR mark-shot-upload (1)
